# NJEN environment example — placeholders only. NEVER commit real secrets.
# Copy to .env.local for local work. All .env files except this one are git-ignored.
#
# RULES
# - Variables WITHOUT the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix are server-only and never reach the browser.
# - Variables WITH the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix are compiled into browser code: they are public.
#   Never put a secret, service-role key, password or connection string behind NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# - Real values live only in the hosting provider's encrypted environment settings (NJEN-owned).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Currently used by the application
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Shows unpublished sections (see lib/sections.ts) for private staging review.
# Server-only. Leave unset or false in production.
# NJEN_PREVIEW_UNPUBLISHED=false

# robots.txt disallows all crawling unless this is true (see app/robots.ts).
# Set to true ONLY in the production environment at launch.
# NJEN_ALLOW_INDEXING=false

# Absolute site URL, e.g. https://example.org (no trailing slash). Server-only.
# Enables canonical URLs and the sitemap. Leave unset until NJEN confirms the
# production domain (register C13); the sitemap stays empty while unset.
# NJEN_SITE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PLANNED — not implemented yet. Documented so setup is quick once NJEN provides
# access. Do not add real values here, and do not create accounts to fill them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Supabase / PostgreSQL (register D4/T1) — Week 2
# Server-only. The database connection string used by Payload and by future
# application services. Never expose to the browser.
# DATABASE_URI=postgresql://[USER]:[CLIENT TO PROVIDE SECURELY]@[HOST]:5432/postgres
#
# SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are now READ BY THE APPLICATION:
# lib/early-access-store.ts uses them to store Early Access signups. With both
# unset the site builds and renders exactly as it does today, and the Early
# Access form says plainly that nothing was saved. Setting BOTH, after applying
# db/migrations/0002_early_access_signups.sql, turns real lead capture on.
# Nothing else is needed — not Resend, not DNS, not a domain.
# SUPABASE_URL=                     # e.g. https://[PROJECT-REF].supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=        # server-only; full access; never NEXT_PUBLIC_
#
# Browser-side Supabase access is NOT used at launch. Only add these if and when
# NJEN approves direct browser access, and only with Row Level Security in place:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Payload CMS (register T3) — Week 2
# Server-only. PAYLOAD_SECRET signs sessions/tokens; treat it like a password.
# PAYLOAD_SECRET=
# PAYLOAD_ADMIN_EMAIL=              # first staff account, created manually at setup

# Resend transactional email (register D5/T5) — Week 3
# Server-only.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# NJEN_EMAIL_FROM=                  # verified sending address on the NJEN domain
# NJEN_EMAIL_TO=                    # where contact/submission notifications go (register C8)

# Sentry monitoring (register D6/T7) — Week 3/4
# SENTRY_DSN is server-side. NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN is intentionally public: a DSN
# only allows sending events. The auth token is server-only and used at build time.
# SENTRY_DSN=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=                # build-time source map upload; never in client code

# Plausible analytics (register D6/T6) — Week 3/4
# The site domain is public by nature; there is no secret.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=

# Newsletter provider — OPEN (register T5a). No variables until NJEN decides.
# Payment provider — POST-LAUNCH (register T10). No variables at launch.
